{"Expired deadline skips workers - if next_step.join() or an earlier flusher worker consumes the timeout, the break exits the loop before later workers are even checked, causing join(timeout=...) to return while some shard workers are still alive and still flushing Redis to Kafka, overlapping with shutdown or the next consumer instance": 0.9487683176994324, "Negative process count crashes startup - click's plain int type accepts values like --flusher-processes -1, which reaches SpanFlusher with a negative process count, builds an empty process map, and then the shard assignment indexes a missing process, crashing the process-spans consumer during startup": 0.9296774864196777, "Killed children are not reaped - when a flusher worker is unhealthy, the code kills it and overwrites the stored process reference with a new worker, but the parent never joins the killed child, so repeated worker restarts can leave zombie processes behind and eventually exhaust process resources": 0.9049752354621887, "Cluster memory queried per worker - SpansBuffer.get_memory_info() returns memory for the whole Redis cluster, not only the buffer's assigned shards, so with multiple flusher workers the loop runs the same cluster-wide memory query once per worker on every submit, multiplying Redis INFO load unnecessarily": 0.8742437362670898}